# Bounded reconnect lifecycle

The accepted authentication, Retina/full-panel and dependency-cache work is
merged into main (root d34a110, Client 060e6424). Implement this follow-up on
reconnect-lifecycle, independently of unrelated platform research.

## Contract

- Automatic recovery remains available across Linux login/logout and Mac
  login/logout, worker replacement and temporary network outages.
- Authenticate once per setup context. Retry topology/display readiness using
  that context, not another password conversation. A consumed launch token or
  an explicitly expired/replaced context needs fresh authorization.
- Invalid credentials, permission/ownership denial and TLS rejection are
  terminal; never repeatedly submit a known-rejected password.
- Every reconnect control request checks the configured wait deadline. At
  Ask timeout, no new requests begin until Keep Waiting. An already in-flight
  bounded request may finish; it cannot start another request or complete the
  reconnect behind the unanswered prompt. Disconnect/quit cancels the gate.
- Mac HTTP 503 topology/display readiness retains an authorized setup token
  only within its original expiry, peer and identity binding. Invalid requests,
  permission denial, ownership changes, failed launch, cancellation and failed
  response delivery still revoke it. No larger token pool or prolonged expiry.
- No protocol fields, credentials storage, bookmark polling, capture, codec,
  transport or input behavior changes. Linux Host is unchanged.

## Verification

Run executable fake-clock retry-policy tests, reconnect integration/source
guards, HTTP status classification checks, Mac real TLS synthetic readiness
retry tests and existing authorization/replay/permission cleanup tests.
Build on hosted builders using the canonical runbooks. Record builds separately
from live acceptance: user should test login/logout, unavailable Host Ask/Wait/
Disconnect, and terminal authentication failure. Do not induce a production
account lockout or interrupt a live session for automated testing.

## Candidate status

1.0.116 hosted builds passed: Mac Host 35074853150, Mac Client 35074420641,
Ubuntu Client 35074423798. Both Mac packages are signed/notarized. Exact source,
hashes, gates and the earlier cancellation-test finding are recorded in HANDOFF.
An expired request is revoked by its monotonic deadline as well as the network
cancellation flag. A password challenge paused behind Ask is restarted after
Keep Waiting; a transport completed after the deadline is torn down before
waiting. Local source/unit/CI checks and root CTest pass. The operator reports
manually installing Host 1.0.116 and explicitly authorized merging this work
into main. Live recovery acceptance is still pending; installation alone is
not a functional test pass. Existing packages retain their candidate qualifier.
